        "text": "While it's still possible to copy digital goods, NFTs make it very easy to determine whether someone selling or distributing a copy of a digital asset is its real owner. NFTs are primarily used to represent ownership of digital items, although they can also certify ownership of physical items in the real world. Similar to cryptocurrencies, NFTs can be traded in open marketplaces, but it's worth noting that the value of each NFT is unique. Both cryptocurrencies and NFT prices are volatile, so be cautious if you invest in them. NFTs have the potential to be one of the critical components of a blockchain powered Digital Economy and Web3. They could be used in many different fields, such as video games, digital identity, licensing, ticketing, membership certificates, fine art, and fractional ownership of assets.",
